#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1380.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199262} :activity/id #uuid "ee989efc-2e02-5faf-9663-d0e67a72db66" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050741 :topic/id #uuid "62cde46f-1bc8-533b-b62a-02ec7aac97f3" :topic/math-academy-id 4174} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199262 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199458 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we discuss a concept analogous to *center of mass* that applies to rotating bodies.\n\nRecall that the *center of mass* of a plane lamina is defined as the point $(\\bar{x},\\bar{y})$ in the coordinate plane where the entire mass of the lamina could be concentrated to produce the same *total moment* about the coordinate axes as the original laminar. \n\nAnalogously, the **radius of gyration** of a plane lamina is the distance $R$ from an axis of rotation $L$ that the entire mass $M$ of the lamina would need to be concentrated to produce the same *moment of inertia* as the original lamina. \n\n![](images/c9/c9999bf30a93a857db731488739f0a640edc7b91de907cd772b777489a011fb8.png)\n\nTo derive an explicit formula for the radius of gyration, recall that the moment of inertia of a particle $P$ of mass $m$ at a distance of $r$ from an axis of rotation equals\n\n$$\nmr^2.\n$$\n\nSo, for a particle of mass $M$ at a distance of $R$ from the axis of rotation $L,$ the moment of inertia about $L$ is given by\n\n$$\nMR^2.\n$$\n\nThe radius of gyration is defined as the distance $R$ that a particle of mass $M$ must be placed to give the same moment of inertia as the original lamina. Therefore, it is the solution to the equation\n\n$$\nI = MR^2,\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about $L.$\n\nRearranging this equation, we find that the radius of gyration is given by\n\n$$\nR = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I}{M}}.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "9694de04-ca38-5d55-a60f-6663ca34e7cf" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5074 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "76c2c5a5-4cc8-5b16-af7c-3ebae501b962" :step/math-academy-id 31767 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199368}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199344 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198417 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198059 :question/id #uuid "88848c23-66fe-5937-958c-28d73b593d99" :question/math-academy-id "e-12487"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049331}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198651} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198665} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235554} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281676} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281677} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281678} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435469} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435471} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435472} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435473} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435475}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"} :step/id #uuid "b8d3d2ed-b979-53cc-a718-ce66bcb92672" :step/math-academy-id 44959 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199351}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199348 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198419 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198061 :question/id #uuid "fa3e8249-cb9f-50f6-a56f-6f311d101de6" :question/math-academy-id "e-12495"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198663} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198957} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281681} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284392} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284393} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284394} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284396} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284397} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369922} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369943} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435474} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435477}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Radii of Gyration Using Polar Coordinates"} :step/id #uuid "4f7fed02-59a7-5116-a7d3-2d07448fbbfa" :step/math-academy-id 45033} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199351 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198421 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198063 :question/id #uuid "5245b67a-8beb-512d-b3c8-2d38db797703" :question/math-academy-id "e-12507"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198664} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198956} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281682} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281684} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281685} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281686} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326719} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369929} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369936} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370880} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435470} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435476}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"} :step/id #uuid "b3e8808b-6d9a-533e-98f7-fae6b2f81961" :step/math-academy-id 45077 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199348}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199368 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199498 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we'll limit the axis of rotation to the $x$-axis, the $y$-axis, and the origin. We summarize the key results below:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ of a lamina about the $x$-axis is given by $R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}},$ where $I_x$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ of a lamina about the $y$-axis is given by $R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}},$ where $I_y$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ of a lamina about the origin is given by $R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}},$ where $I_0$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about the origin." :tutorial/id #uuid "096487a4-3e7b-571a-94b9-ec4e84d689bd" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7823 :tutorial/title "A Summary of Key Results"} :step/id #uuid "b488dfc8-1a77-5eca-8218-1163bb51565d" :step/math-academy-id 45253 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199344}}] :activity/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Plane Lamina" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186198500}]}
